\f0\fs24 \cf0 # ADR-002: RabbitMQ Event Processing\
\
## Status\
\
Accepted\
\
## Context\
\
The system must support asynchronous operations such as:\
\
- Reservation confirmation\
- Reservation reminders\
- Kitchen notifications\
- Future SMS and Email integration\
\
Direct synchronous service calls would tightly couple the modules.\
\
## Decision\
\
RabbitMQ will be used as the message broker.\
\
Business modules will publish events.\
\
Consumers will process these events independently.\
\
Example:\
\
Reservation Created\
        \uc0\u8595 \
RabbitMQ\
        \uc0\u8595 \
Notification Service\
\
## Consequences\
\
Advantages:\
\
- Loose coupling\
- Better scalability\
- Asynchronous processing\
- Easier feature expansion\
\
Disadvantages:\
\
- Additional infrastructure\
- Eventual consistency\
- Slightly higher complexity\
\
## Justification\
\
RabbitMQ aligns with modern event-driven architecture and supports future scalability requirements.}